      "id": "claim_1311bde23f634fc0aa3ffa2720da972a",
      "statement": "GitHub login issues a signed state carrying a hashed nonce stored in a short-lived state cookie and redirects to GitHub's authorize URL; the callback validates the state nonce against the cookie, exchanges the code, enforces an organization login gate, persists the token, and issues a signed session JWT in the session cookie.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/dashboard/routes.py#L456-L544",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f1ae0243aa2d04a76c3fae0eddd1d1f307f420ea209fc288fcd6ecdff9659b91:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_412bfb0cc40b4b7aa5523becfe654a6b",
      "statement": "Every mutating dashboard request is guarded by the router-level dependency require_same_origin_for_mutations, which passes GET/HEAD/OPTIONS and bearer-token-only requests but rejects cookie-authenticated mutations whose Origin/Referer is not in the dashboard allowlist with a CSRF error.",
